Z||000000||Flash Box||12-02-2000||09:56 AM||||The other day I cleaned my Fiero all up especially the engine compartment, I started it to warm it up some and I noticed the famous orange glow coming from the engine compartment, do I run and get the marshmallows, NO!!, I shut the car off pop the lid and by this time the orange glow is out. I noticed a couple of leaves that I missed getting out of the engine compartment so like an idiot I reach down in there to pull them out needless to say I now have a burn mark across the back of my hand that goes from my knuckle to my wrist. On a good note it was only one of the leaves that caught fire and nothing was damaged.  <P>------------------<BR>"5 out of 4 people have a problem with fractions."||||reg||6
Z||000001||batboy||12-02-2000||10:09 AM||||I say it was love that made you stupid!||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-02-2000||11:23 PM||||That's ok, years ago I grabbed an exhaust manifold to see if it was hot. It's amazing just how hot they get in 30 seconds.||||reg||9
Z||000003||JohnnyK||12-03-2000||01:38 AM||||30 seconds?? Mine burnt the crap out of my hand in less than 10. I was impressed (and then concerned)||||reg||1
